# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.node and docker/Dockerfile.python.
#
# Two jobs. The first is size: the workspace carries several node_modules trees
# and five Python virtualenvs, and every one of them is rebuilt inside the image
# from a lockfile, so shipping them into the context only slows the build.
#
# The second job matters more. A file that reaches the context can end up in an
# image layer, and an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
# Nothing holding a credential may enter: the .env files, Terraform variable
# files and state, and the AWS profile directory are excluded for that reason
# and not for size. Keep new secret-bearing paths on this list.

# Dependency trees and virtualenvs -- rebuilt from lockfiles inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Build output -- rebuilt inside the image
dist
**/dist
.nx
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
coverage
**/coverage

# Never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/terraform.tfvars
infrastructure/terraform/state
infrastructure/terraform/**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
.aws
**/*.pem
**/*.p12

# Repository plumbing the build never reads
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/*.log
